# Trade Companion — web app

Real-time trading alerts and watchlist management. Next.js 14 App Router,
React 18, TypeScript, Zustand, Tailwind. Deploys to Vercel on merge to
`master`. Also runs inside Electron (`electron/`).

The people using this are day traders watching it during market hours. A bug
here is not a broken page — it is a missed catalyst on a live position.

## Layout

| Path | What's in it |
|---|---|
| `app/page.tsx` | Tab shell. 1 Alerts, 2 Watchlist, 3 Scanner, 4 Themes, 5 Settings |
| `app/api/` | Server-side route handlers (keeps API keys off the client) |
| `app/pop/` | Pop-out windows (alertbar, watchlist, scanner, mascot, alerts) |
| `components/` | All UI. One file per surface, no nesting |
| `hooks/` | One hook per data source. This is where alerts are born |
| `lib/` | Pure helpers — dedup, filtering, colors, formatting |
| `store/useStore.ts` | The entire Zustand store. Single file, ~600 lines |
| `types/index.ts` | `Alert`, `AppConfig`, `Watchlist`, everything |

## Backends it talks to

- **Azure Functions** — `tradecompanion3.azurewebsites.net/api` (the "hub"),
  configurable per user via `config.hubUrl`
- **SignalR** — live alert push (`hooks/useSignalR.ts`)
- **News hub** — separate JWT-authed SignalR (`hooks/useNewsHub.ts`)
- **Airtable** — RSS / YouTube / Substack feeds
- **Cosmos** — watchlist + settings sync (`hooks/useCosmosSync.ts`)

Local dev hits CORS on all of these. `lib/proxyUrl.ts` rewrites those origins
to Next rewrite paths when on localhost — always wrap outbound URLs in
`proxyUrl()`. Do not add a new backend origin without adding it to both
`PROXY_MAP` and `next.config.js` rewrites.
